# Shell scripts and container files must keep LF endings regardless of the
# checkout platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `entrypoint.sh` runs inside a Linux container; with CRLF
# endings the kernel reads the shebang as `/bin/sh\r` and the container dies
# with "no such file or directory" -- an error that names neither the file nor
# the real cause. Git on Windows converts by default (core.autocrlf=true), so
# without this the demo breaks for exactly the people ADR-006 wrote it for:
# someone cloning fresh on Windows and running `docker compose up`.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
